It is my lunch break at work.
I would like to book an appointment with a dentist.
Therefore, I call a local clinic.
A receptionist answers the phone.
"Do you have time on Thursday?" he asks.
"We have an available appointment at quarter past two."
I look at my phone and check my calendar.
"Yes, Thursday at quarter past two suits fine," I say.
Then he asks for my phone number.
"My number is twelve, thirty-four, fifty-six, seventy-eight," I answer.
He notes down the number, and we say goodbye.
Now I have my first dentist appointment in Denmark, and it feels good.
